\f4\fs26 Agent Jones had the techs were separated and tied into interrogation chairs in adjoining interview suites. All upholstery and bindings were made from uncomfortable scratchy plasti-carbon fibre both for strength and ease of cleaning. Blood and chunks of tissue easily hosed off the fabric, facilitating a speedy turnover of prisoners during busy times. Most interrogators did not carry a set of medieval instruments of torture, a pharmacy of pain amplifying drugs or some cliched psychology text book. The method of choice was the time honoured belting the crap out of the prisoner until he confesses. Agent Jones however, carried a chef\'92s knife roll filled with gleaming stainless steel knives, curved saws, drills and diabolical mechanical devices with spinning cutting wheels and pointy bits. He loved a good trope.\
\'93What the fuck? There is no need for this.\'94 Screamed Tech idiot 1. \'93What do you want to know?\'94\
\'93Tell me about the cleaner.\'94 Agent Jones approached with a slender probe and slipped it into the webbing of his fingers, drawing out a scream of fear and extreme pain.\
\'93I don\'92t know. He stopped to help the blank and we told him to fuck off. That\'92s it.\'94\
\'93What did he look like?\'94 The second probe introduced to the webbing of his other hand.\
\'93A Eurasian male, about 25 years old, dark hair and dressed in a pair of busted-ass overalls. I think he was a cleaner because of the logo.\'94\
\'93Logo? Why didn\'92t you tell me this before?\'94\
\'93You didn\'92t ask. You\'92re the fucking intelligence agent. I am just a tech. We love gadgets. We love slinking around in the dark, planting surveillance devices and the odd bomb. Investigation is your gig.\'94\
\'93What did it say?\'94 Agent Jones was excited, he might live to the end of the day yet. \'93The Logo?\'94\
\'93I can\'92t remember. Jack\'92s cleaning? Maybe.\'94\
\'93Let me assist your memory.\'94 The probes sticking out of either hand were connected to a transformer and a current was sent into his body. He screamed and screamed, but no relief came. \'93Do you remember now?\'94 The current was increased and the screams intensified, his steaming body jerking and jumping in spastic spasms. \'93How about now, fuck-face? Huh? Put my contract on the line will you?\'94 Agent Jones allowed the current to flow for another minute or more before it was interrupted and the screams died down. \
\'93Let me think! Please, just let me think!\'94 The tech was panting and frothing at the mouth, his sweat soaked torso squirming. \'93Jack, Jack\'92s Crack, Jack\'92s Crackers Cleaning? No, No. Cracker Jack Cleaning. That\'92s it. Cracker Jack Cleaning.\'94 \
\'93There, that wasn\'92t so hard.\'94 Agent Jones was very happy and decided to celebrate by torturing his ex-colleague for several more hours. Confirmation of \'93Cracker Jack Cleaning\'94 was gained when the process was repeated with Tech No 2. They were then killed. He did not have to kill them and he probably shouldn\'92t have, but they were witnesses to his incompetence and they had to be eliminated. His career was far more important than their two lousy lives.\
The interlink yielded very little information to Agent Jones, but after a few hours of on-line inquiries he managed to nail down a couple of addresses that looked promising. 
